    "imports-format": "Every in-repo file a module specifier names: relative specifiers, `export ... from` re-exports, and workspace package names resolved to the entry point or subpath file.",
    "workspace-main": "`@acme/utils` is a workspace package (root package.json `workspaces: [\"packages/*\", \"apps/*\"]`) whose package.json `main` is src/index.ts; there is no tsconfig `paths`, so only the workspace declaration resolves it.",
    "workspace-barrel": "The name comes from @acme/utils's entry src/index.ts, a barrel that re-exports it from format.ts or math.ts (`export *`); the call target is the defining file.",
    "workspace-namespace": "`import * as utils from '@acme/utils'`; `utils.sum` and `utils.clamp` come through the barrel's `export * from './math'`.",
    "workspace-exports": "@acme/logger has no `main`: its `exports[\".\"]` condition `types` names ./src/index.ts (the `import` condition's dist/ is a build output not in the repository).",
    "workspace-exports-subpath": "`@acme/logger/levels` is the `exports` subpath `./levels`, mapped to ./src/levels.ts.",
    "workspace-subpath": "`api-client/lib/users` names a file inside the unscoped workspace package api-client, which has no `exports`, so the subpath is a path in the package.",
    "workspace-class": "`new Logger()` with Logger imported from @acme/logger types the local, so `log.record` is Logger.record.",
    "re-export": "`export ... from` lines are imports of the re-exported file.",
    "lodash": "`_.capitalize` is lodash, not the unexported capitalize in @acme/utils's format.ts.",
    "not-a-workspace": "tools/scripts has a package.json named @acme/scripts, but no workspace glob matches tools/: the import is an external package.",
    "global": "`fetch` is the platform global.",
